A||||7||Alex4mula||Day at drag races (no Fieros :-(  )||||1||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||02-05-2001||03:09 PM||||Visited yesterday my local drag strip track. A lot of fun. No I did not raced my car but plan to do it soon. Found out they have test & tune days when you can run for only $10. Found it cheap. <BR>Mainly the races where on Detroit iron like Camaros, Chevelles, etc. Was disappointed with the Mustang Cobras. Two of them only did 14.9 & 15. Shouldn't they be 13s cars? There was a (turbo I guess) new Toyota Corolla that did better with a 14.5. New Ford Lightning's are fast. Did 13.0 just like a stock C5 Vette and a Viper. A late turbo Supra was doing 13.5. Couple of Integras doing 15.5-15.9. Front wheelers have a hard time hooking up. And the sentimental  winner was an 80s VW wagon that did 24s! After seeing that I guess I won't feel bad if I go and don't do a good job...<BR>Question: How do you do a good burnout to heat tires in a standard car? Some of the newer cars had problems in that area compared to the old ones (with locking mech. I guess).<BR>Tks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||02-05-2001||03:33 PM||||I have VERY limited experience on the strip but the often cited advise was -don't do a burn out with street tires. Wrong formulation of rubber you get no gain from "warming" them up, also you can splash water up into the wheelwells||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||02-05-2001||04:55 PM||||My brother uses some spray on stuff(forgot the name of it) on the wheels of go-carts that makes them real sticky that last for a little while.  I wonder if it's still a tire compound issue.  Maybe it would make a street tires sticky.??||||reg||5
Z||000003||1FST2M6||02-05-2001||05:12 PM||||the Carollas have a TON of performance options open to them.. the 4AGZE supercharged motors drop right in making them low 14-high 13second cars. <P>as for the burn outs.. get DOT Drag Radials (BF Goodrich or NITTO NT555R) and don't waste your money destroying your street tires. they will just get hot and seperate causing a crappy ride and possible catastrophic failure if you have a fiero you'll need a line lock or quick reflexes to stay in the burn out box.. my auto matic will power brake the 235-40s but after a few second once they start to heat up they jjust over power the front brakes and push me across the parking lot. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||firstfiero||02-05-2001||08:13 PM||||   Those Ford lightnings are crazy fast for a truck   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !!! Handle as good as any sports car also. My father in law took me around corners That you were only supposed to do 35 at about 120 mph. I struggle to do 60 or so in my 86 se around the same corners. A Truck just no supposed to handle like that!  86se||||reg||10
Z||000005||Alex4mula||02-06-2001||03:33 PM||||Drag radials??? Mmm... Heard of them. Maybe if I get hooked on and my wife let me I may consider them. I'm planning to buy new 17"s rims so I can have the drags on the 15"s. But first would have to fix my noisy CV joint before braking it...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan86gt3.8||02-07-2001||11:37 AM||||Viper only in the 13's somethings majorly wrong!  The stock vette 13's are good was it a 6 speed?  It might have got a little better time with a really good driver...  Ya 4.6 modulars and some cobras are slow as hell.  I have ben known to beat them at the stoplight races many a time!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||02-07-2001||12:42 PM||||yep.. BF-G  and NITTO both make DOT approved drag radials.. Mickey Thompson will be releasing theirs soon. if you can fin a set of 14" wheels that would be better than the 15s.. your rotating weight will be closer to th center of the wheel for faster spool-up and less weight. 215-60-14 ar $130ea and last a long time on our cars... or a 205-60-15 yokohama A032 they are super sticky too.. but a bit higher price.  good luck breaking any of those loose! ||||reg||1
